# ==========================================
# GOOGLE ANTIGRAVITY IDE COMBINED RULES
# Optimized for: Fast/Planning Modes & Roo Code Style
# Stack: React.js & Node.js (Express)
# ==========================================

# --- ANTIGRAVITY WORKSPACE & MODE CONTROLS ---
- WHEN IN FAST MODE: Execute immediate, localized code changes without generating extensive boilerplate descriptions or empty placeholder files. Focus entirely on direct code insertion and fast terminal verification.
- WHEN IN PLANNING MODE: Halt execution until an implementation plan artifact with an explicit task list tree is generated. Wait for a user comment/approval before touching files.
- If a loop error occurs in Fast Mode (e.g., a terminal compile error repeats twice), automatically shift context to draft a mini-plan to self-heal the error.
- Utilize the integrated Browser-in-the-Loop feature to verify frontend styling layout and routing changes autonomously after major sprints.

# --- CRITICAL TOKEN & PERFORMANCE SAVINGS ---
- NEVER overwrite or rewrite an entire massive file just to change a few lines of code. Use localized edits or search-and-replace blocks.
- Break massive single files into modular components or utility functions if they exceed 400 lines of code.

# --- NODE.JS / EXPRESS CODE STYLE ---
- Use clean, modern ES Modules syntax (import/export) instead of CommonJS (require).
- Every asynchronous route handler must leverage try/catch blocks and pass errors cleanly using next(error).
- Group backend components into dedicated `routes/` and `controllers/` directories.
- Always append explicit HTTP status codes to responses (e.g., res.status(200).json(), res.status(201), res.status(400)).

# --- REACT.JS CODE STYLE ---
- Build component structures using modern arrow functions (`const Component = () => {}`).
- Maintain highly modular structures; split any component if it exceeds 150 lines of code.
- Always define explicit dependency arrays for useEffect hooks. Never leave them empty unless explicitly intending to run once on mount.
- Use descriptive variable names for hooks (e.g., const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(false)).
- Use semantic HTML tags styled with Tailwind CSS utility classes.

# --- DEVELOPMENT & TESTING ---
- When creating backend API endpoints, always provide the exact fetch/axios snippet needed on the frontend to call it.
- Before installing any new npm packages, check the existing package.json first to ensure we do not create duplicate dependencies.
